1. site.air.temperature = 10 °C | engineering assumption, no source | temperate NW-European annual mean... The user answered: Approve all except: 1. site.air.temperature = 8 C instead of 10 C. Everything else as proposed. = "Approve all except: 1. site.air.temperature = 8 C instead of 10 C. Everything else as proposed.", because the user's answer to ask_user; do not ask it again
Assumption A1 [confirmed, user]: Time zone of the daily demand series = "UTC", because The demand files give bare dates with no offset and the brief names no site, so no zone can be read from the files. The user instructed UTC as a clearly labelled, UNCONFIRMED assumption; it is not a value from any file.; source: {"origin": "user message"}
Assumption A2 [confirmed, user]: site.air.temperature = "8 \u00b0C", because The brief names no site and gives no air conditions; the user set 8 °C in place of the proposed 10 °C.; source: {"origin": "user message"}
Assumption A3 [confirmed, agent]: site.air.relative_humidity = "0.8 (-)", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: temperate NW-European annual mean relative humidity; the brief gives no site or air data.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A4 [confirmed, agent]: site.air.pressure from site elevation = "elevation 0 m -> 101325 Pa (ISA, ISO 2533:1975, set by gemini)", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief names no site or elevation, so sea level (0 m) is assumed; gemini set the ISA pressure.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A5 [confirmed, agent]: site.fluid.dissolved_gas.N2 and .H2S = "0 mol% each", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief's produced gas is CH4 80 mol% + CO2 20 mol% only (p.2), which closes the composition to 100 mol%, so N2 and H2S are zero.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A6 [confirmed, agent]: site.fluid.sand_concentration = "0 g/m3", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief states no sand or solids content of the brine.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A7 [confirmed, agent]: demand.heating.return_temperature = "50 \u00b0C", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief fixes only the 100 °C heating supply; a 50 °C return is a typical DH design return, colder than the supply.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A8 [confirmed, agent]: demand.heating.return_pressure = "4 bar(g)", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief gives no consumer return pressure.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A9 [confirmed, agent]: demand.cooling.return_temperature = "26 \u00b0C", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief fixes only the 20 °C cooling supply; a 26 °C return is warmer than the supply, as a chilled-water return must be.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
Assumption A10 [confirmed, agent]: demand.cooling.return_pressure = "4 bar(g)", because engineering assumption, no source, approved by the user: the brief gives no consumer return pressure.; source: {"origin": "agent assumption"}
