Assumption E2 [confirmed, agent]: economics.analysis_period = 25 yr = "25 yr", because Cost catalogue row analysis-period-dea-2019-geothermal-dk (verified, 2019). Approved by the user.; source: {"row": "analysis-period-dea-2019-geothermal-dk", "year": 2019, "document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv", "publisher": "PlanEnergi and GEUS"}
Assumption E3 [confirmed, agent]: economics.capex.drilling = 1844.74 EUR/m = "1844.74 EUR/m", because Cost catalogue row drilling-nl-2013-3000m (verified, 2013), the row nearest the 2500 m reference depth. Approved by the user.; source: {"row": "drilling-nl-2013-3000m", "year": 2013, "document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv"}
Assumption E4 [confirmed, agent]: economics.capex.production_pump = 1.5457689466758628 EUR/W electric = "1.5457689466758628 EUR/W electric", because Cost catalogue row production-pump-schlagermann-2023-332kwel (verified, 2023). The row is per W electric (motor rating) while the key is per W of shaft power: per W of shaft power the cost is about 10-15 % higher (cost-sources.md batch 3). Approved by the user.; source: {"row": "production-pump-schlagermann-2023-332kwel", "year": 2023, "document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv", "publisher": "Schlagermann and Reinicke, Geothermal Energy 11:33"}
Assumption E5 [confirmed, agent]: economics.revenue.heat = 114.555 EUR/MWh; economics.revenue.cold = 103.547 EUR/MWh = "heat 114.555 EUR/MWh, cold 103.547 EUR/MWh", because Cost catalogue rows heat-price-nl-cap-2026 (verified, 2026) and cold-price-no-2017 (secondary, 2018). Approved by the user.; source: {"rows": ["heat-price-nl-cap-2026", "cold-price-no-2017"], "document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv"}
Assumption E6 [confirmed, agent]: economics.energy.electricity = 115.01546759736655 EUR/MWh; economics.energy.gas = 37.507733798683276 EUR/MWh; economics.carbon.price = 57.4757281553398 EUR/t = "electricity 115.01546759736655 EUR/MWh, gas 37.507733798683276 EUR/MWh, carbon 57.4757281553398 EUR/t", because Cost catalogue rows electricity-nl-eurostat-2024-band-id, gas-nl-eurostat-2024-band-i4 and carbon-price-eu-ets-esma-2026. Approved by the user.; source: {"rows": ["electricity-nl-eurostat-2024-band-id", "gas-nl-eurostat-2024-band-i4", "carbon-price-eu-ets-esma-2026"], "document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv"}
Assumption E7 [confirmed, agent]: All other economics keys set from the cost catalogue's recommended row (capex, opex fixed, opex per_energy for boiler/electric_boiler/heat_pump/chp, opex.variable.chemical, accounting) = "catalogue recommended rows", because Cost catalogue knowledge/cost-sources.csv, recommended row per key by the selection rule (sourced, verified, latest year). Approved by the user in the economics question.; source: {"document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv"}
Assumption E8 [confirmed, user]: economics.revenue.subsidy.* left open (no subsidy) = "open", because The user's answer to the economics question: no Dutch subsidy, because the site is not in the Netherlands as far as they know.; source: {"origin": "user message"}
Assumption E9 [confirmed, user]: economics.opex.variable.waste_disposal left open = "open", because The user's answer to the economics question: a French low-level radioactive waste tariff does not fit a geothermal plant.; source: {"origin": "user message"}
Assumption E10 [confirmed, agent]: economics.opex.per_energy.compression_chiller / absorption_chiller / adsorption_chiller left open = "open", because The cost catalogue has no row for the chillers' per-energy O&M; the user left the open keys open. A plant that uses a chiller needs the user's price for it.; source: {"document": "knowledge/cost-sources.csv"}
Assumption E11 [confirmed, user]: utilities.electricity.co2_intensity left open = "open", because The user answered 'leave open'; the brief states no utilities and the catalogue's Ember rows for this key carry no value.; source: {"origin": "user message"}
